
%!includeconf: conf.t2t

= WrithDeck =

A distraction-free text editor for writerdecks (homemade prototypes or
computers dedicated to writing), as a GUI or straight in a terminal/TTY,
from a single executable with no install. Markdown/txt2tags syntax
highlighting, a modal command mode, writing stats, a timer and stopwatch,
light/dark themes. Also ported to Android, ASM, C, DOS, ESP32, Lua and web.

[images/writhdeck.png]

[github.com/luginf/writhdeck https://github.com/luginf/writhdeck] -
[binaries on itch.io https://farvardin.itch.io/writhdeck]

= WrithDeck everywhere =

The same editor, ported to very different machines: Android (Kotlin), ESP32
(embedded JimTcl, VGA output and PS/2 keyboard), assembly, uxn, web (a single
HTML file) and C. The C version produces a tiny static binary with no
dependencies, for very old hardware (photo: a Toshiba 2180).

[images/writhdeck-c.jpg]

[Android https://github.com/luginf/writhdeck-android] -
[ESP32 https://github.com/luginf/writhdeck-esp32] -
[ASM https://github.com/luginf/writhdeck-asm] -
[uxn https://github.com/luginf/writhdeck-uxn] -
[web https://github.com/luginf/writhdeck-web] -
[C https://github.com/luginf/writhdeck-c]

= SciTE plugins =

Lua scripts for the [SciTE https://www.scintilla.org/SciTE.html] editor: a file
finder and browser with content and tag search, recent files, snippets, a
heading navigator (txt2tags and Markdown), txt2tags/Markdown formatting from
the context menu, expression evaluation, and Zettelkasten-style
``[[target|ID]]`` links with backlinks.

[images/scite.png]

[github.com/luginf/scite-plugins https://github.com/luginf/scite-plugins]

= Zettelium =

A Zettelkasten note-taking app in txt2tags syntax, packaged as a single
self-contained HTML file (no server, no install). ``[[target|id]]`` links
with a backlinks panel, live syntax highlighting and preview, tag search,
several local repositories through the File System Access API. Built on
the same principles as WrithDeck, with which it shares the same plain-text
files.

[images/zettelium.png]

[Try it online https://luginf.github.io/zettelium-web/zettelium.html] -
[github.com/luginf/zettelium-web https://github.com/luginf/zettelium-web]

= KOReader plugins =

Custom plugins for the [KOReader https://koreader.rocks/] e-reader,
including ``txt2tagsreader`` (native reading of ``.t2t`` files) and
``bookstats`` (reading statistics, word count).

[github.com/luginf/koreader-plugins https://github.com/luginf/koreader-plugins]
